<title>INDIA: Indian May exports grew 8-9 pct yr/yr - minister.</title>
<headline>Indian May exports grew 8-9 pct yr/yr - minister.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's merchandise exports grew at a rate of about eight to nine percent in May over the same month in 1996, Commerce Minister Bola Bulli Ramaiah said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Exports in May are about eight to nine percent over the year,&quot; Ramaiah told reporters in the capital.  </p>
<p>Merchandise exports in May 1996 were valued at $2.63 billion, up 13.56 percent over the same month in 1995.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
